Package: BSSUnfoldR
Type: Package
Title: Neutron Spectrum Unfolding for Bonner Sphere Spectrometers
Version: 0.2.1
Date: 2026-09-17
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Konstantin",
           family = "Chizhov",
           email = "kchizhov@jinr.ru",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1591-4289")))
Author: Konstantin Chizhov [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Konstantin Chizhov <kchizhov@jinr.ru>
Description: A port of the Python package 'bssunfold' (Radiationsafety/
    bssunfold) to R. Provides tools for unfolding neutron spectra measured
    with Bonner sphere spectrometers, including a Detector R6 class with 60+
    unfolding algorithms (iterative, Bayesian, maximum-entropy,
    Krylov/regularization, statistical regularization, sparse/dictionary,
    optimization/meta-heuristic, parametric and pipeline/ensemble families;
    see the reference index), Monte-Carlo uncertainty estimation, a
    max_neutron_energy cutoff on every method, comparisons and benchmarking
    utilities, ggplot2 visualisation, and dose-rate calculation using
    ICRP-74, ICRP-116 and NRB99-2009 conversion coefficients plus seven
    published Bonner-sphere response functions (GSF, PTB, LANL, JINR,
    FERMILAB, EURADOS, IHEP).
